# Google Workspace CLI (gws)

`gws` is installed at `{{ gws_bin }}` (also symlinked to `{{ gws_binary_install_dir }}/gws`).

## Before any gws command

```bash
{{ gws_bin }} auth status
```

If auth fails, tell the user to run:

```bash
{{ gws_bin }} auth login -s {{ gws_auth_scopes }}
```

## How to use gws in Cursor

| Method | When to use |
|--------|-------------|
| **Custom skills** | Gmail search/list workflows — start with `gws-gmail-search` |
| **Upstream skills** | Send, reply, triage, calendar agenda — `gws-gmail-*`, `gws-calendar-*`, etc. |
| **Shell** | Run `{{ gws_bin }}` commands directly via Bash |

> `gws` does **not** ship an MCP server (it was removed upstream). Use skills + shell.

## Gmail quick reference

```bash
# Unread inbox summary
{{ gws_bin }} gmail +triage

# Search with any Gmail query (sent, labels, dates, keywords)
{{ gws_bin }} gmail +triage --query 'in:sent label:work newer_than:7d' --max 50

# Read a message
{{ gws_bin }} gmail +read --id MESSAGE_ID --headers

# Send email (confirm with user first)
{{ gws_bin }} gmail +send --to user@example.com --subject "Hi" --body "Hello"
```

For detailed search workflows (sent mail + label + date range, keyword search, pagination),
use the **gws-gmail-search** skill.

## Upstream skills already installed

The role installs 100+ skills from [googleworkspace/cli](https://github.com/googleworkspace/cli).
Key Gmail skills:

| Skill | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `gws-gmail` | Full Gmail API surface |
| `gws-gmail-triage` | Inbox summary with `--query` |
| `gws-gmail-read` | Read message body/headers |
| `gws-gmail-send` | Send email |
| `gws-gmail-reply` | Reply to thread |
| `gws-gmail-forward` | Forward message |
| `gws-shared` | Auth, flags, output formats |

## Safety

- Search and read operations are safe to run without confirmation.
- **Always confirm** before send, reply, forward, delete, or label changes.
- Use `--dry-run` on write operations when unsure.
